    hook: "More businesses fail from cash flow problems than from bad products, bad teams, or bad ideas. A business can be profitable on paper — showing positive net income on its financial statements — while simultaneously running out of cash and being forced to close. This seems impossible until you understand the timing difference between profit and cash. Cash flow is the oxygen of business. Without it, even a healthy business dies quickly.",
