    hook: "Research consistently shows that 70-80% of jobs are never publicly advertised — they're filled through connections. LinkedIn's own research found that 85% of jobs are filled through networking. The uncomfortable truth: the quality and breadth of your professional relationships may matter more to your career outcomes than your talent, credentials, or even hard work. Networking is not glad-handing and collecting business cards — it's the strategic cultivation of genuine relationships that create mutual value over time.",
